<title>UK: LME copper ends little changed in late trading.</title>
<headline>LME copper ends little changed in late trading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Copper prices held steady during late inter-office trading, after earlier volatility sparked by contractions in some spread backwardations.</p>
<p>Three months LME copper fell through $2,200 and then $2,200 support before stabilising at $2,183 a tonne, a $61 loss from Tuesday.</p>
<p>At 1900 GMT copper was last indicated at $2,180/2,185 with cash/threes at $245/255, sharply down from Tuesday's $335.</p>
<p>Other metals were little changed.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
